# AIG Architecture Rules

Read `AGENTS.md` for full context. This rule enforces the hard module
boundaries every change must respect.

## Forbidden imports

- `lib/aig/**` MUST NOT import from `lib/db/**`, `lib/arcade/**`, `lib/auth/**`,
  or I/O packages — **except** documented orchestrators (`executor.ts`, `expire.ts`)
  and `repair.ts` (may import `ai` + `lib/ai/anthropic.ts` only).
- `app/**` and `components/**` MUST NOT import `lib/db/**`, `lib/arcade/**`,
  or `lib/auth/server.ts`. Use API routes, `lib/auth/client`, or `lib/display/**`.
- `@arcadeai/arcadejs` MUST NOT be imported outside `lib/arcade/**` (scripts exempt).
- `better-auth` MUST NOT be imported outside `lib/auth/**` and `app/api/auth/**`.
- `process.env` MUST NOT be read outside `lib/env.ts` (config/test/script paths,
  plus the Next 16 `proxy.ts` edge entry, are exempt). CI enforces via
  `pnpm check:boundaries`.
- Nothing outside `lib/logger.ts` constructs a `pino` logger.

## Side-effect placement

| Concern | Location |
| ------- | -------- |
| Intent / tool_call / mutation DB | `lib/db/queries.ts` |
| Toolkit connections + resolution | `lib/db/connection-queries.ts` |
| Org bootstrap DB | `lib/db/provision-queries.ts` |
| Workspaces DB | `lib/db/workspace-queries.ts` |
| Schema + migrations | `lib/db/schema.ts`, `lib/db/migrations/` |
| Arcade SDK | `lib/arcade/**` (singleton via `client.ts`) |
| Better Auth | `lib/auth/server.ts`, `lib/auth/client.ts` |
| Session + workspace context | `lib/auth/session.ts` |
| LLM plan + label | `lib/ai/plan-agent.ts`, `lib/ai/labeler.ts` |
| LLM repair | `lib/aig/repair.ts` via `lib/ai/anthropic.ts` |
| HTTP JSON helpers | `lib/api/http.ts` |
| HTTP route handlers | `app/api/**/route.ts` only |
| Intent OAuth sync + SSE fingerprint | `lib/intent/authorization-sync.ts` |
| Connections list-time Arcade re-check | `app/api/connections/route.ts` (`syncPendingConnections`) |
| Pipelines (templates promoted from runs) | `lib/db/pipeline-queries.ts`, `lib/aig/pipeline.ts` |
| Insights (read-only stats) | `lib/db/insights-queries.ts` |
| Approval policies | `lib/aig/approval-policy.ts` (pure), `lib/db/approval-policy-queries.ts` (DB), `app/api/approval-policies/**` |
| Team/member settings | `lib/db/team-queries.ts`, `app/api/team/**`, `components/settings/team-panel.tsx` |
| Add-action / replan | `app/api/intents/[id]/mutate/route.ts`, `lib/db/queries.ts` (`insertHumanToolCall`) |
| Session-gate proxy (Next 16) | `proxy.ts` (was `middleware.ts`) |
| Import boundary CI | `scripts/check-boundaries.ts` (`pnpm check:boundaries`) |

## TypeScript hygiene

- No `any`. Use `unknown` + zod parse, or a precise generic.
- `import type` for type-only imports (`verbatimModuleSyntax` enforces).
- Zod schemas live next to the route handler / function that uses them, or
  in `lib/aig/types.ts` if they are domain primitives.
- Result types: prefer `{ ok: true, data } | { ok: false, error }` for any
  function that can fail in a non-exceptional way. Throw only for invariants.

## UI conventions

- All modals and confirmations use `components/ui/dialog.tsx` (Radix Dialog).
- `window.confirm`, `window.alert`, and `window.prompt` are forbidden anywhere
  in `components/**` and `app/**`. Destructive actions go in a Dialog with the
  `destructive` button variant.

## State machine

- Any change to intent status MUST go through `assertTransition()`.
- New transitions require a unit test in `tests/unit/state.test.ts`.

